SUMMARY:Volunteer Day: Help Sort & Pack Food for Homeless Support & Commun
 ity Programs
DESCRIPTION:Sai Dham Canada Toronto Volunteer Group\nJoin us this Saturday
  to make a real difference in our local community! We are looking for enth
 usiastic volunteers to help sort and pack food donations for our homeless 
 outreach program and families in need across North Etobicoke.\nWhether you
  can give an hour or stay for the entire afternoon\, your time directly he
 lps ensure fresh\, nutritious food reaches those who need it most.\n\nWhat
  to Expect\n12:30 PM – 12:45 PM | Arrival & Orientation\nWe start with a
  quick 15-minute overview of our operations\, safety guidelines\, and task
 s for the day.\n12:45 PM – 3:30 PM | Sorting\, Packing & Hampers\n\nVolu
 nteers will help sort perishable and non-perishable food items\, pack food
  hampers\, and assist with general food bank activities.\n\nFlexible Commi
 tment: Volunteers are welcome to stay for a minimum of 1 hour or hang out 
 and help until 3:30 PM (or up until we close at 4:00 PM!).\nWhat to Bring 
 / Wear\nClothing: Comfortable\, seasonal clothing Footwear: Closed-toe sho
 es (sneakers or work boots) are required for safety in the warehouse.\n\nB
 ring your energy and readiness to team up with awesome fellow volunteers!\
 n\nGetting Here & Parking\nAddress: 31 Steinway Blvd\, Etobicoke\, ON M9W 
 6N3\nEntrance: Please head to the side entrance of the building upon arriv
 al.\nParking is available on-site.\n\nHow to Join\nRSVP right here on Meet
 up so we know how many volunteers to expect. If you have any questions bef
 ore attending\, feel free to drop a message in the discussion section or r
 each out directly.\n\nWe look forward to seeing you there!
